# DevOps and Monitoring Guide

> **Related Rules**: [Conventional Commits](conventional-commits.mdc) | [Release Management](release-management.mdc) | [Semantic Release Workflow](semantic-release-workflow.mdc) | [Testing Standards](testing-standards.mdc)

This guide covers DevOps practices, monitoring strategies, logging, deployment processes, and observability for the EduHub application.

## Deployment Architecture

### Environment Structure
```
EduHub Environments:
├── Development (develop branch)
│   ├── Auto-deployment on push
│   ├── Docker Compose local setup
│   └── Feature testing
├── Staging (staging branch)
│   ├── Pre-production testing
│   ├── Integration testing
│   └── User acceptance testing
└── Production (production branch)
    ├── Semantic release triggers
    ├── Blue-green deployment
    └── Monitoring and alerting
```

### Docker Configuration

#### Multi-Stage Docker Builds
```dockerfile
# Dockerfile-edu (optimized for production)
FROM node:20-alpine AS deps
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json yarn.lock ./
RUN yarn install --frozen-lockfile --production=false

FROM node:20-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY . .
RUN yarn build

FROM node:20-alpine AS runner
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV production
RUN addgroup --system --gid 1001 nodejs
RUN adduser --system --uid 1001 nextjs

COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public
COPY --from=builder --chown=nextjs:nodejs /app/.next/standalone ./
COPY --from=builder --chown=nextjs:nodejs /app/.next/static ./.next/static

USER nextjs
EXPOSE 3000
ENV PORT 3000

CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

#### Development vs Production Compose
```yaml
# docker-compose.yml (development)
services:
  frontend-nx:
    build:
      context: frontend-nx
      dockerfile: Dockerfile-dev
    volumes:
      - ./frontend-nx:/app
